# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Presses Activate in the [aspect gump for the armor and the held item, every run.
# Activated gear loses its aspect when you die. The names cannot tell when to activate: a
# piece taken off and put back loses its aspect while the others keep theirs, and the
# aspect only works with every piece on (user check, 2026-10-19). So it always presses.
# The server answers each press: "Lyric aspect armor activated." and "Eldritch aspect
# activated." when it takes, 5 Arcane Essence each, "Your armor is already of that
# aspect." and "That equipped item is already of that aspect." when it was on already,
# and those cost nothing (user check, 2026-10-19). The gump rows are what the server keeps
# for the character, so nothing is remembered here.
#
# The weapon row and the spellbook row share one active aspect: activating either turns
# every weapon and spellbook to it (user check, 2026-10-19). Neither the item in hand nor
# the skills tell which one a character wants, hybrids carry both. So set both rows to the
# same aspect, and aspect_hand_row picks the one pressed.
#
# Gump 2424293173, Activate buttons 8 weapon, 13 spellbook, 17 armor, each pressed twice:
# the first press answers "Click again to confirm." (Razor recording and user check,
# 2026-10-19). Button 102 leaves the unlocked list for the rows, after the "Dress Suite -
# Aspect" script by thisideasucks on outlands.uorazorscripts.com.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ config
#
#   config__aspect_hand_row
#      The gump row pressed for the held item.
#        0  none: the hand is left alone
#        1  the weapon row
#        2  the spellbook row
#      Both share one aspect, so with the two rows set alike either does.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__aspect_hand_row 2


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ wait
#
#   wait__aspect_gump
#      How long the gump may take to open, or to come back after a press.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! wait__aspect_gump 1000


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ setup
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Whatever was still moving items has to finish before the gump is answered.
while queued
    wait wait__short
endwhile

say "[aspect"
waitforgump 2424293173 wait__aspect_gump

if ingump "Show Only Unlocked" 2424293173
    gumpresponse 102 2424293173
    waitforgump 2424293173 wait__aspect_gump
endif

# The armor first, then the hand, the order the screen takes. The server answers each in
# the Journal: activated, or already of that aspect.
if gumpexists 2424293173
    gumpresponse 17 2424293173
    wait wait__short
    waitforgump 2424293173 wait__aspect_gump
    gumpresponse 17 2424293173
    waitforgump 2424293173 wait__aspect_gump

    if config__aspect_hand_row = 1
        gumpresponse 8 2424293173
        wait wait__short
        waitforgump 2424293173 wait__aspect_gump
        gumpresponse 8 2424293173
        waitforgump 2424293173 wait__aspect_gump
    elseif config__aspect_hand_row = 2
        gumpresponse 13 2424293173
        wait wait__short
        waitforgump 2424293173 wait__aspect_gump
        gumpresponse 13 2424293173
        waitforgump 2424293173 wait__aspect_gump
    endif

    gumpclose
else
    overhead "[ aspect, miss ]" 254
    if config__sysmsg = 1
        sysmsg "Aspect: the [aspect gump did not open." 88
    endif
endif
